@startuml SubmitConsent

title Submit Consent API Sequence

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox
actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Consent Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "m_user" as m_user
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "t_consent" as t_consent
    database "t_user_consent" as t_user_consent
end box
user -> page: Display consent; optionally answer later
activate page
page -> api: POST v1/consent/submit (displayed version, isRead=true, optional result)
activate api
api -> app: [**SubmitConsentCommandHandler**] Process request
activate app
note over app, infra
    Omission of result means read-only; null, a string or a number is not an omitted boolean. Duplicate
    consentIds return 400 E10001; do not apply the same consent twice or pick one answer. Invalid body/ordinary
    headers return 400 before BEGIN. Missing/malformed/invalid Bearer credentials return the same 401 E10002
    `Invalid or expired access token.`
    Use typed bound UUID arrays, timestamps and booleans, never string-concatenated SQL.
    userId/createdBy/updatedBy are the authenticated server-derived user id. Each item maps its
    query/INSERT/UPDATE result to consentId, consentVersion, isRead, readAt and result. Return data.consents in
    original request order, even though processing is sorted. No stored token/hash or internal evidence id is
    returned.
end note
    note over app, infra
        Lock order: BEGIN READ COMMITTED -> lock ACTIVE authen.m_user by verified userId FOR UPDATE -> capture fresh
        UTC now after the lock -> recheck JWT expiry and the ACTIVE stored access-token hash/user/expiry -> validate
        the complete current consent set -> process evidence in ascending consentId order -> COMMIT before 200.
        Logout/reset and other writes for this user take the same user lock. A waiter must check token revocation
        after acquiring the lock; do not authorize from a pre-lock snapshot or transaction-start NOW(). Missing
        user/token or expired JWT returns 401 after ROLLBACK, with no evidence changes.
    end note
app -> app: Create request context and requestId
app -> domain: Validate non-empty consents, UUID/version/isRead=true, result presence/type, duplicate ids
domain -> app: Return validation
alt Invalid body or ordinary headers
    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
    api -> page: Validation failure
else Valid body
    app -> app: Verify Bearer JWT signature/issuer/audience/exp/sub
    alt Missing, malformed or invalid JWT
        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
        api -> page: Authentication failure
    else Verified JWT
        app -> app: userId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT; consentIds = unique submitted ids
        app -> infra: BEGIN READ COMMITTED
        note over app, infra
            Compare the complete returned id set with the request before any evidence write. A
            hidden/missing/future/expired consent or inactive type returns 404 E10004 `Consent not found.` A displayed
            version unequal to the returned current version returns the existing 409 E10003 `Consent version is not the
            current version.` Reject the whole batch, never a partial success. Eligibility is evaluated at that one
            validation snapshot; later policy publications affect subsequent calls while existing evidence is retained.
            Existing evidence is keyed logically by (userId, consentId, consentVersion). The schema has no unique
            constraint; serialize all calls under the user lock so concurrent display/answer requests cannot both
            insert. For legacy multiple ACTIVE rows, select the newest created_at, then greatest id as a deterministic
            canonical row. Update/return only that row; preserve all older rows and all other versions. Pending/inquiry
            must use the same canonical choice when their own API review is delivered; do not infer acceptance from any
            arbitrary older duplicate. Register creates a new user and cannot race an authenticated request for that
            same uncommitted user.
            All evidence writes are one transaction. A later item/DB failure rolls back earlier item changes. Timeout
            before COMMIT rolls back and returns 408 E90001; unexpected failure rolls back and returns generic 500
            without a new bizCode. Return 200 only after COMMIT succeeds, including all-no-op batches. Lost response
            after commit does not undo evidence; retrying the same displayed version preserves its first read timestamp
            and is a no-op when the answer is unchanged. Old versions and inactive-type evidence are never deleted or
            rewritten by this call.
        end note
        alt Transaction work completes
            app -> infra: QUERY - Lock the user
            infra -> m_user: QUERY - Lock the user
            activate m_user
                note right of m_user
                    SELECT
                        u.id as user_id
                    FROM authen.m_user u
                    WHERE u.id = '<sequence.userId>'
                    AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    FOR UPDATE -- user lock precedes token and evidence reads
                end note
                m_user -> infra: Return ACTIVE user row or no row
            deactivate m_user
            infra -> app: Return ACTIVE user row or no row
            alt ACTIVE user returned
                app -> app: Capture fresh UTC now after user lock; recheck JWT exp
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check the active access token
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check the active access token
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching token or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching token or no row
                alt Stored token valid and JWT still unexpired
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Get active consents
                    infra -> t_consent: QUERY - Get active consents
                    activate t_consent
                        note right of t_consent
                            SELECT
                                c.id as consent_id,
                                c.consent_version
                            FROM consent.t_consent c
                            WHERE c.id = ANY ('<sequence.consentIds>'::UUID[])
                            AND c.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                            AND c.effective_at <= '<sequence.now>'
                            AND (c.expired_at IS NULL OR c.expired_at > '<sequence.now>')
                            AND EXISTS (
                                SELECT 1
                                FROM consent.m_consent_type ct
                                WHERE ct.id = c.consent_type_id
                                AND ct.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                            )
                            ORDER BY c.id
                        end note
                        t_consent -> infra: Return eligibleConsentIds and current versions (ACTIVE type included)
                    deactivate t_consent
                    infra -> app: Return eligibleConsentIds and current versions (ACTIVE type included)
                    app -> domain: Compare complete eligible id set and all displayed versions before writes
                    domain -> app: Return eligibility/version validation
                    alt Any requested id missing or hidden by type/status/time
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 Consent not found.
                        api -> page: Consent unavailable
                    else Any displayed version differs from current version
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 Consent version is not the current version.
                        api -> page: Reload displayed versions
                    else All submitted ids and versions valid
                        loop Each consent in ascending consentId order
                            app -> app: resultSpecified = property present; result = explicit boolean or false for insert
                            app -> app: Read-only never overwrites an existing answer
                            app -> infra: QUERY - Get existing user consent
                            infra -> t_user_consent: QUERY - Get existing user consent
                            activate t_user_consent
                                note right of t_user_consent
                                    SELECT
                                        uc.id as user_consent_id,
                                        uc.consent_id,
                                        uc.consent_version,
                                        uc.result,
                                        uc.is_read,
                                        uc.read_at
                                    FROM authen.t_user_consent uc
                                    WHERE uc.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                                    AND uc.consent_id = '<sequence.consents.consentId>'
                                    AND uc.consent_version = '<sequence.consents.consentVersion>'
                                    AND uc.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                                    ORDER BY uc.created_at DESC, uc.id DESC
                                    LIMIT 1
                                end note
                                t_user_consent -> infra: Return canonical evidence (id, result, isRead, readAt) or no row
                            deactivate t_user_consent
                            infra -> app: Return canonical evidence (id, result, isRead, readAt) or no row
                            alt No canonical ACTIVE row for user/consent/version
                                app -> infra: INSERT - Create user consent
                                infra -> t_user_consent: INSERT - Create user consent
                                activate t_user_consent
                                    note right of t_user_consent
                                        INSERT INTO authen.t_user_consent (
                                            created_by,
                                            user_id,
                                            consent_id,
                                            consent_version,
                                            result,
                                            is_read,
                                            read_at
                                        )
                                        VALUES (
                                            &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                            &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                            &#39;<sequence.consents.consentId>',
                                            &#39;<sequence.consents.consentVersion>',
                                            &#39;<sequence.consents.result>', -- explicit result, or false for a new read-only row
                                            TRUE,
                                            &#39;<sequence.now>'
                                        )
                                        RETURNING id as user_consent_id, consent_id, consent_version, result, is_read, read_at
                                    end note
                                    t_user_consent -> infra: Return new evidence id, consentId, version, result, isRead, readAt
                                deactivate t_user_consent
                                infra -> app: Return new evidence id, consentId, version, result, isRead, readAt
                                app -> app: responseItem = inserted evidence; isRead=true, readAt=now
                            else Canonical row already read and result omitted or unchanged
                                app -> app: responseItem = existing evidence; no INSERT or UPDATE; preserve result/readAt
                            else Canonical row unread or explicit answer changed
                                app -> app: userConsentId = canonical evidence id; preserve first readAt if already read
                                app -> infra: UPDATE - Update user consent
                                infra -> t_user_consent: UPDATE - Update user consent
                                activate t_user_consent
                                    note right of t_user_consent
                                        UPDATE authen.t_user_consent
                                        SET
                                            updated_by = '<sequence.userId>',
                                            updated_at = '<sequence.now>',
                                            result = CASE WHEN '<sequence.consents.resultSpecified>'::BOOLEAN THEN '<sequence.consents.result>'::BOOLEAN ELSE result END,
                                            read_at = CASE WHEN is_read THEN read_at ELSE '<sequence.now>'::TIMESTAMP END,
                                            is_read = TRUE
                                        WHERE id = '<sequence.userConsentId>'
                                        AND user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                                        AND consent_id = '<sequence.consents.consentId>'
                                        AND consent_version = '<sequence.consents.consentVersion>'
                                        AND row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                                        AND (NOT is_read OR ('<sequence.consents.resultSpecified>'::BOOLEAN AND result IS DISTINCT FROM '<sequence.consents.result>'::BOOLEAN))
                                        RETURNING id as user_consent_id, consent_id, consent_version, result, is_read, read_at
                                    end note
                                    t_user_consent -> infra: Return updated evidence id, consentId, version, result, isRead, readAt or no row
                                deactivate t_user_consent
                                infra -> app: Return updated evidence id, consentId, version, result, isRead, readAt or no row
                                alt Guarded UPDATE returned one row
                                    app -> app: responseItem = updated evidence
                                else Guarded UPDATE returned no row
                                    break Abort entire request on internal consistency failure
                                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                    app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                                        api -> page: Batch failed; every earlier item rolled back
                                    end break
                                end
                            end
                            app -> app: Collect responseItem by original request position
                        end loop
                        app -> infra: COMMIT
                        infra -> app: Return committed batch
                        note over app, infra
                            This detailed revision remains in-review and includes no backend implementation.
                            Answering later calls the same endpoint with result=true or false. An existing answer survives a read-only
                            request. An already-read version keeps its original read_at: do not write read state again. An already-read
                            read-only request, or the same explicit answer on already-read evidence, performs no UPDATE at all
                            (including audit columns). An answer change may update result while preserving read state/timestamp.
                            No body userId or token-supplied role changes the target user. Any ACTIVE authenticated user may submit
                            their own consents; no administrator role is required and no assignment-table lookup authorizes this
                            endpoint.
                            A new evidence row stores result=false when result was omitted, is_read=TRUE and read_at=now. Optional
                            rejection is also read. Required rejection/read-only is allowed for an existing user and stays pending until
                            both read and accepted (Q8/Q9); this API adds no service-access gate.
                            For an existing unread row, mark it read once and set read_at=now; preserve its current result when result
                            is omitted. For an already-read row, preserve read_at even when NULL in legacy data; do not invent a
                            first-read time. For an explicit answer change, update result only as part of the guarded evidence update.
                            resultSpecified records presence independently of its boolean value, so explicit false is never treated as
                            omission. The SQL predicate prevents no-op UPDATEs; Application skips the UPDATE entirely when already read
                            and result is omitted/unchanged.
                            New-row INSERT, existing-row UPDATE and no-op are mutually exclusive per item. UPDATE guards id, user_id,
                            consent_id, consent_version and ACTIVE state; an unexpected zero-row guarded update is an internal
                            consistency failure, causing whole-batch ROLLBACK and generic 500, not a partial 200. An empty id array
                            never reaches SQL because the request is invalid.
                        end note
                        app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Submit Consent Success; data.consents = original request order
                        api -> page: Return consentId, consentVersion, isRead, readAt, result
                    end
                else Stored token missing/revoked/expired or JWT expired during wait
                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Authentication failure; no evidence change
                end
            else Missing or inactive user
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                api -> page: Authentication failure; no evidence change
            end
        else Timeout before COMMIT
            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
            app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
            api -> page: Whole batch timed out
        else Unexpected pre-commit failure
            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
            app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
            api -> page: Whole batch failed
        end
    end
end
deactivate app
deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
